  <title id="bdl28sparsitypriors-title">Laplace, scale mixture and horseshoe priors and their prior predictive functions</title>
  <desc id="bdl28sparsitypriors-desc">Three rows. Top: Laplace densities with scale 0.1 (peak 5), 1 and 10, and prior predictive functions that are flat at zero for 0.1, a narrow band for 1 and a wide spread for 10. Middle: scale mixtures of a wide and a narrow zero-mean Gaussian with weight pi on the wide one equal to 0.1, 0.5 and 0.9; the peak at zero drops as pi grows, and the prior predictive functions spread more for larger pi. Bottom: horseshoe densities with sigma squared 0.02, 1 and 50, all with a pole at zero and heavy tails; the prior predictive functions are flat for 0.02 and 1 and form a band around zero for 50, with occasional large excursions.</desc>
